{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[llm-prompts overlay / Pass-1] code-review-tests.md removes the parsed `outputs: code_review_findings` front-matter field — prompt/contract DRIFT (a non-human consumer branches on this key, so it is CONTRACT, not prose).\n\nEvidence:\n- `outputs` is a canonical front-matter contract key (prompts_frontmatter.py:62, in the closed FRONT_MATTER_KEYS set), parsed into `Prompt.outputs` (prompts.py:271).\n- Consumed programmatically: code_review/batch_runner.py:162-166 REJECTS any overlay whose `prompt.outputs != \"code_review_findings\"` (`_FINDINGS_SCHEMA`) → with the field removed, `prompt.outputs` is None, so a project-criterion overlay at this path raises LLMError \"expected outputs 'code_review_findings', got None\". Also workflow/runs.py:305-314 binds `output_schema=prompt.outputs` for single_turn and raises PromptError on empty outputs; editor_contracts.py:110 `_schema_fields(prompt.outputs)`; prompt_library.py:134; prompts.py override-drift check.\n- Every sibling code-review-pass overlay declares `outputs: code_review_findings` (code-review-security/docs/a11y/i18n/… all line 7).\n- Tests assert the value: tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py:133 `assert p.outputs == \"code_review_findings\"`; test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py:42; test_code_review_scope_intent.py:175; test_code_review_deletion_impact.py:140 — these break on removal.\n- The repo's OWN eval spec seeds this identical diff as an expected finding: eval_specs/code-review-llm-prompts.eval.yaml:26-41 (`id: R-frontmatter-field-removed`, `expect: finding`, `mode: required-frontmatter-field-removed`)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785710560405468001,"uuid":"f358eb71-5fe0-474c-8c42-20bed331dacd"}